v 3
d stdotplot. Individual follow-up histories of st data as a connected dot plot
d
d {cmd:stdotplot} draws one horizontal line per subject from multiple-record,
d multiple-failure {cmd:stset} data, with markers for events of interest,
d competing events, censoring and entry. Follow-up segments can be coloured
d by a time-varying categorical variable, and time-varying weights (e.g.
d inverse probability weights) can be shown as line width or colour
d intensity. Competing codes before the end of follow-up are always marked,
d so misspecified data are easy to spot.
d
d Author: Barna Szabo, Karolinska Institutet
d Requires: Stata 15 or later (line widths in points need Stata 16)
d Distribution-Date: 20261119
f stdotplot.ado
f stdotplot.sthlp
